{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_chip

    One chip of the filter line's second row: a criterion in force that the line
    does not show, as a link to the listing with that one criterion dropped and
    every other part of the request kept, so it works with no JavaScript. The
    listing's clients intercept it by its action (dim-chip-remove) and read what
    it drops from data-param: a custom field's parameter (cf_<id>), chip, cat,
    or period for both bounds of the start-date range. The label and the address
    are the server's (category_toolbar::chips()); a client paints the chips of
    every answer with the same markup and composes neither. The cross is drawn,
    and the visually hidden words after it make the link's name say what a
    press does.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "param": "cf_12",
        "label": "Online",
        "url": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7&q=resgate",
        "removelabel": "Remover filtro",
        "isperiod": false
    }
}}
<a class="dim-chip" href="{{url}}" data-action="dim-chip-remove" data-param="{{param}}">{{label}} <i class="fa fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">{{removelabel}}</span></a>
